WEBVTT

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:02.786
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Peter wanted to get a job.

00:00:04.368 --> 00:00:10.125
<v><b>Peter:</b></v> I did maths at university and normally, after doing maths at university,

00:00:10.422 --> 00:00:17.656
people get a job in a bank or in IT, but when I finished it was the recession and

00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:19.686
it was very difficult to get a job.

00:00:20.379 --> 00:00:23.640
I was unemployed for quite a long time.

00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:30.339
I was looking for jobs, and I applied for lots of different jobs, but they just answered,

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:34.544
‘Sorry, we don’t want you,’ and I was getting a bit depressed.

00:00:35.117 --> 00:00:39.334
This went on for about four months, and then one day,

00:00:39.359 --> 00:00:44.558
I was on a number forty-nine bus in London – I can even remember where I was sitting –

00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:46.209
and my phone rang.

00:00:46.606 --> 00:00:52.722
I said hello, and a woman said, ‘Hello, you applied for a job with us a few months ago.

00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:53.883
Are you still interested?’

00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:58.337
So I said, ‘Yes, absolutely. I’m very interested.’

00:00:58.806 --> 00:01:04.523
So then she said, ‘We’d like you to come for an interview’… and then, at that moment,

00:01:04.657 --> 00:01:08.156
we got cut off because the bus went into a tunnel.

00:01:08.591 --> 00:01:13.535
And the phone number wasn’t on my phone – it just said ‘unknown number’,

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:20.006
and I couldn’t remember what the name of the company was because I’d applied for so many jobs.

00:01:20.471 --> 00:01:26.547
So I thought, ‘Four months of nothing, and then when they ring, I get cut off.’

00:01:26.962 --> 00:01:35.435
Luckily, they called back the next day, and in the end, I had an interview and I got the job.

00:01:37.407 --> 00:01:40.131
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Sue wanted to see a tiger.

00:01:41.619 --> 00:01:44.772
<v><b>Sue:</b></v> This happened when I was at a conference in Thailand.

00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:51.415
The conference hotel was amazing – it was in a beautiful national park called Khao Yai,

00:01:51.706 --> 00:01:53.085
north of Bangkok.

00:01:53.435 --> 00:01:59.452
We were very busy with talks and meetings most of the time, but we had one free morning,

00:01:59.654 --> 00:02:02.742
and we could choose from different trips or activities.

00:02:03.382 --> 00:02:08.342
I was interested in either a trip to see birds or a trip to see a tiger.

00:02:08.872 --> 00:02:16.356
A tiger, not tigers, because they told us that there was only one tiger in the whole park!

00:02:17.143 --> 00:02:23.543
Well, I chose the tiger trip, because I thought it would be really cool to see a tiger in the wild.

00:02:24.113 --> 00:02:27.194
But we had to leave really early in the morning because we had to travel quite a long way

00:02:27.451 --> 00:02:36.620
to the part of the park where the tiger usually was – the bird trip was nearer the hotel.

00:02:37.275 --> 00:02:43.312
So we tiger-watchers got up at five in the morning, but our guide said that

00:02:43.337 --> 00:02:49.387
we probably wouldn’t see the tiger because, you know, there was only one tiger.

00:02:50.443 --> 00:02:57.534
We finally got there and we spent the whole morning looking for the tiger, but no luck.

00:02:58.145 --> 00:03:04.275
But we saw some nice birds, and it was fun, so when we got back to the conference hotel,

00:03:04.499 --> 00:03:06.728
we felt we’d had a really good morning.

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:11.184
But then the other group got back – the ones who went to see the birds –

00:03:11.452 --> 00:03:17.495
and of course they saw lots of amazing birds, but they also saw the tiger!

00:03:18.588 --> 00:03:21.961
I suppose that day, it wasn’t in its usual part of the park.

00:03:22.344 --> 00:03:28.113
And I thought, ‘Isn’t that typical – you go on the tiger trip and you don’t see the tiger,

00:03:28.358 --> 00:03:31.073
but the people on the bird trip see the tiger!’